From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Porrete <56418580+AndrePorrete@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] goodixtls: no double free when the device is closed during a
 reply

goodix_receive_pack() kept the receive buffer until the reply handlers
returned. Those handlers send the next command with
fpi_usb_transfer_submit_sync(), and gusb runs a nested main loop on the
default context for it, which also dispatches fprintd's D-Bus calls.
When PAM ends a verification (VerifyStop, Release), the device can be
closed inside that loop: goodix_dev_deinit() freed priv->data without
clearing it, and goodix_receive_pack() freed it again on return
("free(): double free detected in tcache 2", seen on CachyOS right
after a pkexec authorization).

Drop the buffer before handling a complete packet, clear it in
deinit, and don't restart the read loop once it was cancelled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libfprint/drivers/goodixtls/goodix.c | 19 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/goodixtls/goodix.c b/libfprint/drivers/goodixtls/goodix.c
index e928e76..de69641 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/goodixtls/goodix.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/goodixtls/goodix.c
@@ -335,6 +335,13 @@ void goodix_receive_pack(FpDevice *dev, guint8 *data, guint32 length) {
       return;
   }
 
+  // The packet is complete: drop the buffer before handling it. The handlers
+  // send the next command synchronously, and gusb then runs a nested main
+  // loop that can dispatch fprintd's D-Bus calls, closing the device
+  // (goodix_dev_deinit) before they return.
+  g_clear_pointer(&priv->data, g_free);
+  priv->length = 0;
+
   switch (flags) {
     case GOODIX_FLAGS_MSG_PROTOCOL:
         fp_dbg("Got protocol msg");
@@ -359,9 +366,6 @@ void goodix_receive_pack(FpDevice *dev, guint8 *data, guint32 length) {
       fp_warn("Unknown flags: 0x%02x", flags);
       break;
   }
-
-  g_clear_pointer(&priv->data, g_free);
-  priv->length = 0;
 }
 
 void goodix_receive_data_cb(FpiUsbTransfer *transfer, FpDevice *dev,
@@ -386,6 +390,12 @@ void goodix_receive_data_cb(FpiUsbTransfer *transfer, FpDevice *dev,
 
   goodix_receive_pack(dev, transfer->buffer, transfer->actual_length);
 
+  // Closed while the reply was handled: don't restart the read loop
+  if (g_cancellable_is_cancelled(priv->transfer_cancel_tkn)) {
+    fp_dbg("transfer cancelled, aborting read loop...");
+    return;
+  }
+
   goodix_receive_data(dev);
 }
 
@@ -1054,7 +1064,8 @@ gboolean goodix_dev_deinit(FpDevice *dev, GError **error) {
       fpi_device_goodixtls_get_instance_private(self);
 
   if (priv->timeout) g_source_destroy(priv->timeout);
-  g_free(priv->data);
+  g_clear_pointer(&priv->data, g_free);
+  priv->length = 0;
   g_cancellable_cancel(priv->transfer_cancel_tkn);
   goodix_shutdown_tls(dev, error);
 
